00:03:02.270 --> 00:03:04.120
- Yeah, I've actually got
a couple of things in mind.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.360
So the first one I wanna talk about

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.260
is working with contractors.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:08.680
Because I work with an editor now

00:03:08.680 --> 00:03:11.720
and he works nearly full-time with me

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.860
though he may be takin'
on some extra contracts

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.200
here and there, on the side.

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:16.590
I've got a few other people who work

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:18.570
nearly full-time, and
then a few people who work

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:19.970
just a few hours a week.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.284
And what a lot of people
always ask, when they start,

00:03:22.284 --> 00:03:24.381
y'know, working with editors,
working with contractors is

00:03:24.381 --> 00:03:28.086
what defines a contractor
who's independent

00:03:28.086 --> 00:03:30.380
from an employee?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.744
And, I mean as you know,
there are many differences

00:03:31.744 --> 00:03:34.425
from the businessperson's perspective,

00:03:34.425 --> 00:03:36.520
an employee, you have to provide benefits,

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.840
you have to provide a
whole host of other things,

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:39.767
you got payroll going,

00:03:39.767 --> 00:03:41.306
and with a contract it's,

00:03:41.306 --> 00:03:44.090
it's really just, y'know, a
1099 at the end of the year

00:03:44.090 --> 00:03:45.190
if you're American,

00:03:45.190 --> 00:03:47.660
and, y'know, either a handshake agreement

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:51.130
or a written contract and
that's kind of it, so,

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.111
from the perspective of the
person running the business,

00:03:53.111 --> 00:03:56.530
it's a lot easier to do the
contractor route, right?

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:58.800
- Often, yeah, and I think you hinted at

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.950
some of the repercussions
that come as a result

00:04:00.950 --> 00:04:02.530
of making that distinction

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:04.250
between someone that you're working with

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:06.300
and saying that they are
an independent contractor

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.250
versus an employee.

00:04:07.250 --> 00:04:10.150
There are of course the benefits
that you have to deal with,

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:12.480
but there are all kinds
of legal protections

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.200
that are afforded for employees

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.124
that are not afforded to
independent contractors

00:04:16.124 --> 00:04:19.490
and there are tons of
tax implications, too.

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:23.090
And I wish I could give you
a really satisfying answer

00:04:23.090 --> 00:04:25.670
that here are the three
things that you must do,

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:28.330
but unfortunately, in most states

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:31.480
and under the federal government, as well,

00:04:31.480 --> 00:04:34.412
there are tons of different standards

00:04:34.412 --> 00:04:36.540
depending on which jurisdiction you're in,

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.476
and on top of that, almost
all of the standards

00:04:38.476 --> 00:04:43.430
have dozens of different
questions that you have to answer

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:46.280
in terms of weighing one way or the other,

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:48.030
and there's no bright line.

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:51.450
Under the federal
guidelines, the US government

00:04:51.450 --> 00:04:53.440
tends to break it up into three sections,

00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:55.070
there's behavioral control,

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.270
there's financial control,

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:58.920
and then there is the relationship itself.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.120
And you're just weighing a
bunch of different factors,

00:05:01.120 --> 00:05:03.004
so in terms of behavioral control,

00:05:03.004 --> 00:05:06.780
if the employer, whether
you're employing an employee

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.961
or an independent contractor,

00:05:07.961 --> 00:05:12.660
has the right to define how
the person does their work,

00:05:12.660 --> 00:05:15.010
that leads to more of an employee

00:05:15.010 --> 00:05:16.777
than an independent contractor,

00:05:16.777 --> 00:05:19.917
whereas if the person
who is doing the work

00:05:19.917 --> 00:05:22.127
can control the manner in which it's done,

00:05:22.127 --> 00:05:24.740
if they use their own tools,

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:27.650
if they have the ability to start and stop

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:28.870
whenever they want,

00:05:28.870 --> 00:05:31.570
that's more indicative of
an independent contractor

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.470
versus an employee.

00:05:33.470 --> 00:05:36.070
On top of it, there is a question of

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:38.026
can they be fired at any time,

00:05:38.026 --> 00:05:41.300
or if they have to stay for
the duration of the job.

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:44.520
And ironically, if you have the
right to fire them whenever,

00:05:44.520 --> 00:05:47.500
that's more of an employee relationship.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.710
Yeah, if you have the
right and the obligation

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:52.160
to finish the job,

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:53.820
that's more of an independent contractor,

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.210
because generally the
independent contractor is more of

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:59.807
a person who is hired for a specific job.

00:05:59.807 --> 00:06:02.110
And that leads to some of
the financial considerations,

00:06:02.110 --> 00:06:04.690
is the second overarching question,

00:06:04.690 --> 00:06:08.870
including the financial
control of the worker.

00:06:08.870 --> 00:06:13.560
If the worker has the
ability to make decisions

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:16.570
that will affect the profitability
of that specific job,

00:06:16.570 --> 00:06:19.440
that is more of an independent
contractor, so, like,

00:06:19.440 --> 00:06:21.400
someone like a video editor, for example,

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.039
they could choose to work
all night and get a job done

00:06:26.039 --> 00:06:29.440
or they could choose to
work whenever they want

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.630
and those are decisions that
can affect the profitability

00:06:32.630 --> 00:06:34.150
of the job.

00:06:34.150 --> 00:06:35.900
- Which makes them more of a contractor?

00:06:35.900 --> 00:06:37.170
- Correct, correct.

00:06:37.170 --> 00:06:39.455
And, y'know, the big one,
traditionally, has been

00:06:39.455 --> 00:06:42.196
are you allowed to work with other people.

00:06:42.196 --> 00:06:47.040
So, part of the classic
independent contractor is like

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:50.344
a plumber that owns Bob's
Plumbing Company and,

00:06:50.344 --> 00:06:52.880
he might work with you and he
might work with a whole bunch

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:53.820
of other people,

00:06:53.820 --> 00:06:56.420
and that kind of financial
freedom is something

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.540
that is indicative

00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:59.220
of an independent contractor relationship.

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:03.050
We think of employees as having one job,

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:05.620
you show up nine to
five, you get a salary,

00:07:05.620 --> 00:07:08.000
and you can't work for anybody else,

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:09.900
you're not really supposed to moonlight.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:12.350
Whereas an independent
contractor is generally someone

00:07:12.350 --> 00:07:14.050
that can work on their own hours,

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:16.020
can work for whomever they want,

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:18.032
and are, they're paid
by the job instead of,

00:07:18.032 --> 00:07:19.962
y'know, a salary.

00:07:19.962 --> 00:07:21.956
- Now I do have a question there.

00:07:21.956 --> 00:07:22.789
- [Host] Sure.

00:07:22.789 --> 00:07:26.190
- Is that determined on whether
or not they have the option

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:27.180
to work with other clients

00:07:27.180 --> 00:07:29.150
or whether or not they literally are?

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.220
So say, y'know, I've
given someone a contract

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:33.410
that effectively buys up all of the time

00:07:33.410 --> 00:07:35.462
that they would be
willing to work normally,

00:07:35.462 --> 00:07:38.024
but they still have the freedom
to work with somebody else

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:39.470
if they have the time

00:07:39.470 --> 00:07:41.234
or if they wanted to work 80
hours a week or something,

00:07:41.234 --> 00:07:43.670
that could still be a
contractor situation, right?

00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:44.680
- Yeah, that's a great question.

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:47.370
And for the most part, it
is based on their ability,

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:48.523
not the actual,

00:07:48.523 --> 00:07:51.002
on the ground status quo
of what has happened, so

00:07:51.002 --> 00:07:56.002
it is the ability to work for other people

00:07:56.344 --> 00:07:59.770
and not just whether, y'know,
they have actually gone out

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:03.570
and gotten other clients
or have chosen not to.

00:08:03.570 --> 00:08:07.500
So, for the most part an
employee is someone that

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.390
doesn't have the ability
one way or the other,

00:08:09.390 --> 00:08:11.907
they are stuck with their employer

00:08:11.907 --> 00:08:15.420
and then that goes right to
the nature of the relationship,

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:17.780
which is the third thing that the IRS

00:08:17.780 --> 00:08:19.610
and the federal government looks to,

00:08:19.610 --> 00:08:22.446
which can be defined by
things like the contract.

00:08:22.446 --> 00:08:25.030
Just because you write in
the contract with someone

00:08:25.030 --> 00:08:27.430
that they are independent
contractor or an employee,

00:08:27.430 --> 00:08:28.610
that's not dispositive,

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.800
but it's certainly good
evidence one way or the other,

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:33.838
because we like to sort of
reward the meeting of the minds

00:08:33.838 --> 00:08:36.980
and we assume that if
you signed the contract

00:08:36.980 --> 00:08:39.330
that you have agreed to those terms

00:08:39.330 --> 00:08:43.196
and that's good evidence
that you have agreed to

00:08:43.196 --> 00:08:45.520
that particular relationship.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.810
And of course,

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:48.390
y'know, the law is what it is.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:50.300
So, just because you've
written it in a contract

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:51.640
doesn't mean it's true.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:54.070
But, y'know, it helps to
define that relationship.

00:08:54.070 --> 00:08:54.903
- Yeah, exactly.

00:08:54.903 --> 00:08:57.530
- And then classically,
along with that relationship

00:08:57.530 --> 00:08:58.990
is the question of benefits.

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.940
And if you provide them to the worker

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.000
then that is another piece of evidence

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:06.290
that they are an employee

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:07.540
rather than an independent contractor.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:09.810
- So if you start providing benefits,

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:11.780
out of the goodness of your
own heart, or something,

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:13.410
that would actually start to move you

00:09:13.410 --> 00:09:15.150
into that employee classification?

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.962
- No good deed goes
unpunished in the legal world.

00:09:17.962 --> 00:09:18.977
(laughing)

00:09:18.977 --> 00:09:20.860
Yeah, that is, that's
definitely how it can go.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.210
- Okay, so I have one final
follow-up question for you,

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:25.950
and this is for people who
just, working on their own,

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:27.720
maybe they have contractors,
maybe they don't,

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:30.150
but I would say the majority
of YouTubers out there

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.753
are sole proprietors.

00:09:31.753 --> 00:09:33.532
At least, the ones in the US,

00:09:33.532 --> 00:09:35.970
or maybe there's an equivalent overseas,

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:38.257
but, y'know, you are the business.

00:09:38.257 --> 00:09:40.132
You are a business, man.

00:09:40.132 --> 00:09:43.160
So the profit of the
business is your paycheck

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:45.130
and that's kind of all there is to it.

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:47.130
So, for those people,

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:49.892
what is the benefit of establishing LLC

00:09:49.892 --> 00:09:53.080
or some other kind of, like,
legal entity for your business

00:09:53.080 --> 00:09:54.840
that separates you from it?

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:56.250
- Yeah, it's a great question,

00:09:56.250 --> 00:09:58.230
and there are a lot of myths about it.

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:00.173
It's really fairly simple, because,

00:10:00.173 --> 00:10:04.167
as you say, as a sole
proprietor, if you incur a debt

00:10:04.167 --> 00:10:08.380
on behalf of your company,
or you do something wrong

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:13.380
and you incur liability for
a contract or some torte,

00:10:13.465 --> 00:10:17.120
the person who's been wronged
can come after you personally.

00:10:17.120 --> 00:10:20.370
So the point of having an entity at all

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.988
is to shield liability so that
if someone files a lawsuit

00:10:23.988 --> 00:10:26.700
they can get all the assets of the company

00:10:26.700 --> 00:10:29.840
but they can't come at you
and your personal assets.

00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:32.730
And so that can be a very important thing,

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.676
it's effectively a type
of insurance, to make sure

00:10:34.676 --> 00:10:38.050
that there's a barrier
between what your company does

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:40.260
and what happens to you.

00:10:40.260 --> 00:10:43.140
And traditionally,
historically, in order to get

00:10:43.140 --> 00:10:44.620
that kind of protection,

00:10:44.620 --> 00:10:47.487
you had to form a regular corporation.

00:10:47.487 --> 00:10:51.790
Which was taxed when profits
come in to the company

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:55.420
and then taxed again when
you take those profits out

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:57.458
and you take a salary as individuals.

00:10:57.458 --> 00:10:59.537
- Yeah, double taxation-based.

00:10:59.537 --> 00:11:00.737
- And that is a very American thing.

00:11:00.737 --> 00:11:03.745
Ironically, a lot of
European countries don't have

00:11:03.745 --> 00:11:06.570
quite that double system
of double taxation

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:08.980
and one thing that most states have done

00:11:08.980 --> 00:11:13.390
is created sort of a hybrid
system which is an entity

00:11:13.390 --> 00:11:15.245
that provides some liability insurance

00:11:15.245 --> 00:11:17.355
but from a tax perspective,

00:11:17.355 --> 00:11:20.597
you don't have to pay double
taxation and it's called,

00:11:20.597 --> 00:11:22.293
what's called a pass-through.

00:11:23.270 --> 00:11:25.260
So, the profits come into the company,

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.170
they aren't taxed at the company level,

00:11:27.170 --> 00:11:29.540
but the taxes at the end of the year

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:32.080
are considered your personal income.

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.578
And so you will pay personal income taxes

00:11:34.578 --> 00:11:37.564
on the profits that come to you.

00:11:37.564 --> 00:11:40.260
So from a creator perspective,

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:43.711
the reason you might wanna create a LLC

00:11:43.711 --> 00:11:47.050
is to shield yourself
from potential liability

00:11:47.050 --> 00:11:49.099
from crazy people that
are out there, or y'know,

00:11:49.099 --> 00:11:52.420
maybe lawsuits that you might get into.

00:11:52.420 --> 00:11:55.849
It allows you to have that
same kind of legal protection

00:11:55.849 --> 00:11:58.700
while only paying taxes once

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:00.490
as income tax when it comes to you.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.150
- [Thomas] So financially, you're still,

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.800
you're still the business, essentially.

00:12:03.800 --> 00:12:05.254
But legally, you are not.

00:12:05.254 --> 00:12:06.780
- Exactly, exactly.

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:08.240
- Now, I've heard that it's a myth that

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:10.803
that liability protection is bulletproof.

00:12:10.803 --> 00:12:13.960
- Yeah, that is definitely the case.

00:12:13.960 --> 00:12:16.350
When you form an entity,
whether it's an LLC

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:20.950
or a corporation, what generally
businesspeople need to do

00:12:20.950 --> 00:12:22.878
is they need to have a
separate business account

00:12:22.878 --> 00:12:25.430
and you have to be very careful about

00:12:25.430 --> 00:12:27.710
separating all of your business things

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:29.410
from your personal things.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.060
Because there's a
concept in the law called

00:12:31.060 --> 00:12:32.617
piercing the corporate veil,

00:12:32.617 --> 00:12:35.029
where the court will say

00:12:35.029 --> 00:12:37.650
"You're not really two separate things,

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:40.793
you've mixed your own money
with the corporation's money

00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:44.009
and as a result we're going to
disregard the corporate form

00:12:44.009 --> 00:12:46.270
and we're just gonna go
after you in particular".

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:49.256
So, y'know, if you have, if
someone has questions about them

00:12:49.256 --> 00:12:52.130
there are some really
good resources online

00:12:52.130 --> 00:12:55.779
that will help you form an
LLC and explain the process

00:12:55.779 --> 00:12:58.910
